Z||000000||TRL46202||01-18-2000||10:18 AM||||There are two conectors at the base of the distributer cap. One (on the right as you look at it)is short and runs straight to the coil the other runs out to the left across the engine and looks to be in some sort of sleeve. I need this the left one because the plug that goes into hte dis. cap doesn't have a clip and is cracked. where can I get a new one????? or for that matter any new wires.<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||01-18-2000||10:57 AM||||Most of the clips on the connectors on my engine are broken and I have never had a problem||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||01-18-2000||12:40 PM||||You local GM dealer should have them just laying around in thier service bay thier nothing really special just a weatherproof GM connector.. if anything maybe a couple bucks at NAPA.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||01-18-2000||03:02 PM||||Tom,  I have been finding (during my rebuild process) that these connectors are very brittle after 13-14 years of heat.  I broke a couple while removing the wiring.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mwbackus||01-18-2000||06:20 PM||||I have noted that the Fiero Store now sells various AC Delco replacement plugs: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/nl/pg1/pg1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/nl/pg1/pg1.html</A> <P>Its nice to know that replacements such as these still exist, although their prices seem a bit extreme.  They do not show this distributor plug in the selection, but I believe it is just a standard weatherproof connector such as those offered by MSD, ACCEL, and others.  Some good info on these connectors can also be found in a previous thread:   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001220.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001220.html</A> <P>Mike||||reg||1
